.TH TABLEPRO 1 2026-11-07 "TablePro 0.1.0-beta.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tablepro \- work with your databases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tablepro
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.RI [ FILE " or " URL ...]
.br
.B tablepro open
.IR FILE " or " URL ...
.br
.B tablepro
.I COMMAND
.RI [ OPTION ...]
.br
.B tablepro
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
TablePro connects to PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQLite, DuckDB, SQL Server, ClickHouse,
Cassandra, ScyllaDB, Redis and MongoDB.
It browses tables, edits rows in place, runs SQL with syntax highlighting,
and reaches servers behind an SSH bastion through the system OpenSSH client.
.PP
Each
.I FILE
is a SQLite or DuckDB database, opened in its own window,
or a SQL file, opened in an editor tab of the connection in front.
A SQL file never runs by itself; with no connection open, the window asks for one.
.PP
Each
.I URL
is a connection URL, such as
.BR postgresql://ada@db.example.com/shop .
TablePro reads the postgres, postgresql, mysql, mariadb, mysqlx, sqlserver, mssql,
mongodb, mongodb+srv, redis, rediss, valkey, valkeys, clickhouse, ch, cassandra,
cql, scylla, scylladb, sqlite, sqlite3 and duckdb schemes.
A URL that goes where a saved connection goes asks before it opens that connection;
any other opens the connect dialog filled from it, where Connect is the user's choice.
A URL never connects on its own.
.PP
A running TablePro opens the files and URLs itself and the new launch exits.
A file whose name is a command's opens with
.B tablepro open
or a path such as
.BR ./query .
.SH COMMANDS
The commands talk to the running TablePro through its MCP server, which
.B Preferences > MCP > Enable MCP Server
turns on.
They read the server's port from the settings and its token from the keyring,
and never start TablePro.
.B tablepro help
.I COMMAND
shows a command's options.
.TP
.B open
Open files and connection URLs, as
.B tablepro
does with no command.
.TP
.B query
Run one SQL statement through a saved connection and print the rows.
.TP
.B connections
List the saved connections the commands can use.
.TP
.BR databases ", " schemas ", " tables
List a connection's databases, schemas, or tables and views.
.TP
.B describe
Show a table's columns, indexes and foreign keys, or its DDL with
.BR \-\-ddl .
.TP
.B export
Print a table as CSV, JSON or SQL INSERT statements, up to 1,000 rows.
.TP
.B status
Say whether TablePro runs, whether its MCP server is on, and whether the command can use it.
.TP
.BI "completion " SHELL
Print the completion script for
.BR bash ", " zsh " or " fish .
The packages install all three.
.TP
.B help
Show the commands, or one command's options.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-new\-window
Open a new window, in the running TablePro when there is one.
With files or URLs, they open in a window of their own.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the commands and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Show the options of the window and of GApplication, and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 1
The database returned an error, TablePro could not be reached, or the output could not be written.
.TP
.B 2
A usage error: an unknown command or option, a bad value, an unknown connection, or a
.I FILE
that does not exist.
.TP
.B 3
Refused: by the connection's External Clients level, Safe Mode, or the MCP server being off.
.TP
.B 4
The statement timed out.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Which messages are logged to standard error, as a tracing filter such as
.BR info " or " tablepro=debug .
.TP
.B TABLEPRO_LOG_FORMAT
.B json
logs one JSON object per line.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tablepro/connections.json
The saved connections: hosts, ports, user names and SSH settings.
Passwords are not in it; they are in the Secret Service keyring.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tablepro/column_widths.json
.TQ
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/tablepro/filter_settings.json
Column widths and filters, kept per table.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tablepro/history.db
The query history and the saved queries, in a SQLite database.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tablepro/workspaces/
The tabs of each connection, and which connections were open at the last quit.
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/tablepro/drafts/
The text of each SQL editor tab.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/tablepro/crashes/
A report of each crash.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/app/app.tablepro.TablePro/ssh/
The control sockets of the open SSH tunnels.
.PP
When unset,
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
is
.IR ~/.config ,
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
is
.I ~/.local/state
and
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
is
.IR ~/.local/share .
Preferences are kept in GSettings, under the schema
.BR app.tablepro.TablePro .
.SH NOTES
In the Flatpak, the commands run inside the sandbox:
.B flatpak run app.tablepro.TablePro
.IR COMMAND .
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/TableProApp/TablePro/issues.
Include the text that Copy Text puts on the clipboard in
About TablePro > Troubleshooting > Debugging Information.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5),
.BR gsettings (1)
.PP
https://docs.tablepro.app
